## UI Rendering Notes

Mapping the new fields onto the Discovery Agent surface:

| Field | Suggested rendering |
|---|---|
| `capabilities` | Chips coloured by `subdomain_class` — core (build-expected) visually distinct from generic (reuse-expected) |
| `coverage_matrix` | The headline view. A matrix or heat strip: one cell per capability, green matched / amber partial / red gap. Replaces "Identified Capabilities" as the primary signal. |
| `excluded_ambient_layers` | Muted footnote row: "Deliberately excluded — not implied by your query" |
| `reuse_mode` | Badge on each component card. `invoke` and `configure` read as cheap; `extend-in-place` and `fork` should carry a visible cost cue. |
| `evidence_awarded` | Expandable under the match score — this is what makes the number auditable instead of asserted |
| `fit_score` + `match_type` | Show together; the band label alone is what let 90%-Partial pass unnoticed |
| `differentiation_flag` | Inline callout on the component card, not buried in risks |
| `mismatch_findings` | Section between Component Layers and Risks — composability is its own concern |
| `gaps` | Never render as an empty region. If empty, state why: "every capability fully matched." |
| `integration_plan` | Ordered stepper below the composition paragraph |
| `sensitivity_points` / `tradeoff_points` | Separate from `risks`; these are escalation candidates for a human architect |
| `org` | Ownership chip on every component card |

